Track 1: Needles Chew the Riverbed
- Story & Context: Before dawn broke across the Bang Nam Phueng canal market, eighty-year-old Somporn accidentally tipped her tuned djembe into the diesel-slicked water just as her drum machine fired a bone-dry 124 BPM tech-house rimshot. Rather than fishing it out, she pressed a contact microphone against the drowning goatskin, capturing an accidental, pressure-soaked 40-hertz resonance that caused the hulls of forty vendor boats to groan in unison. An approaching patrol officer attempted to cite her for an unlicensed generator, but he froze when the warm, subsonic frequency reached his rubber boots, mesmerized into silence while market women rhythmically chopped morning greens to the pulse. Through the dense cloud of frying pandan cakes, Somporn picked up an old bus-driver megaphone and muttered, "Drop the weight before the rope frays."
